From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] calc(), min(), max() and clamp(); :enabled, :read-only, :read-write

Lengths in calc() were not read: Wikipedia sizes its icons with
calc(var(--font-size-medium,1rem) + 4px) (they fell to their 10px
min-width) and hides its buttons' labels in a media query of
max-width: calc(1120px - 1px). A css_length now holds a calc() as an
expression of numbers, lengths and percentages (+, -, *, /, nested
calc(), min(), max(), clamp()): document::to_pixels() evaluates it,
cvt_units() turns its lengths into pixels and leaves its percentages to
calc_percent(), media queries take it as other lengths.

A selector list with :enabled was dropped whole (Codex's
".cdx-button:enabled, .cdx-button.cdx-button--fake-button--enabled"
rules, the quiet buttons' transparent border among them): it matches
form controls that are not disabled; :read-only and :read-write whether
an input or textarea can be edited.
